WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:03.470
-The Supreme Court dealt
President Trump

00:00:03.470 --> 00:00:05.938
yet another major
legal defeat yesterday

00:00:05.938 --> 00:00:09.508
when it rejected a GOP lawsuit
seeking to block Pennsylvania

00:00:09.508 --> 00:00:11.844
from certifying its electoral
votes for Joe Biden.

00:00:11.844 --> 00:00:15.681
So now the GOP is attempting yet
another desperate Hail Mary pass

00:00:15.681 --> 00:00:19.219
to overturn the results,
this one spearheaded by Texas.

00:00:19.219 --> 00:00:21.721
For more on this, it's time
for "A Closer Look."

00:00:21.721 --> 00:00:25.925
♪♪

00:00:25.925 --> 00:00:27.861
-in the waning days of
his presidency,

00:00:27.861 --> 00:00:29.762
Trump has been very
clear about two things --

00:00:29.762 --> 00:00:32.365
one, he's hoping for the courts,
or really anyone,

00:00:32.365 --> 00:00:34.567
to intervene and steal
the election for him.

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:37.636
And two, despite his
catastrophic, sociopathic

00:00:37.636 --> 00:00:40.706
mishandling of the coronavirus
pandemic, he wants credit

00:00:40.706 --> 00:00:43.109
for the arrival of a safe,
effective vaccine,

00:00:43.109 --> 00:00:44.543
which we all know is insane.

00:00:44.543 --> 00:00:47.279
Trump's like those guys who
say, "We're having a baby!"

00:00:47.279 --> 00:00:49.649
You didn't do anything.
All right, you did one thing

00:00:49.649 --> 00:00:51.284
nine months ago,
and by all accounts,

00:00:51.284 --> 00:00:52.818
you didn't do that right either.

00:00:52.818 --> 00:00:55.054
I doubt Trump is
an expert on vaccines.

00:00:55.054 --> 00:00:57.357
I mean, his favorite activities
are honking horns

00:00:57.357 --> 00:00:59.459
and pretending to drive
big trucks.

00:00:59.459 --> 00:01:01.660
He has the intellect
and attention span

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:03.763
of a goldfish
with a head injury.

00:01:03.763 --> 00:01:07.066
Asking Trump to explain how
a vaccine works would be like

00:01:07.066 --> 00:01:10.336
asking a basset hound to find
the hypotenuse of a triangle.

00:01:10.336 --> 00:01:13.138
Trump's not Algernon,
he's the other mouse

00:01:13.138 --> 00:01:16.109
that got the placebo, and who
nobody wrote a book about

00:01:16.109 --> 00:01:17.843
because he just sat
in the corner of the maze

00:01:17.843 --> 00:01:20.612
eating cheese and watching
whatever the mouse version

00:01:20.612 --> 00:01:22.081
of "Judge Jeanine" is.

00:01:22.081 --> 00:01:24.550
"America, it's time to wake up,

00:01:24.550 --> 00:01:27.520
because there's one party
that's dead-set

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:28.988
on destroying your nation.

00:01:28.988 --> 00:01:32.459
I'm speaking, of course,
of the Democats.

00:01:32.459 --> 00:01:35.461
[Bleep] you, Shoe, you should
have told me to take it out.

00:01:35.461 --> 00:01:39.232
It's been on all day.
Side-eyeing me over there.

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:43.269
In fact --

00:01:43.269 --> 00:01:46.372
In fact, for all his desperation
to claim credit for the vaccine,

00:01:46.372 --> 00:01:48.842
it turns out Trump even
botched that, too.

00:01:48.842 --> 00:01:51.611 line:0%
-The Trump administration
reportedly passed

00:01:51.611 --> 00:01:54.347 line:0%
on the opportunity
to lock in a chance

00:01:54.347 --> 00:01:56.549 line:0%
to buy millions
of additional doses

00:01:56.549 --> 00:02:00.619 line:0%
of Pfizer's COVID-19 vaccine
over the summer.

00:02:00.619 --> 00:02:02.388 line:0%
That's according to people
familiar with the matter

00:02:02.388 --> 00:02:04.390
who spoke to
the "New York Times."

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:06.525
The Trump administration
brokered a deal

00:02:06.525 --> 00:02:12.165
for 100 millions doses
for $1.95 billion months ago.

00:02:12.165 --> 00:02:16.635
That's enough to vaccinate only
50 million Americans.

00:02:16.635 --> 00:02:19.872 line:0%
Now the company may not be able
to provide more of its vaccine

00:02:19.872 --> 00:02:22.976 line:0%
to the United States
until next June.

00:02:22.976 --> 00:02:26.312
-What? You had the chance
to buy more vaccine,

00:02:26.312 --> 00:02:29.148
the one thing every expert
has said could be

00:02:29.148 --> 00:02:31.083
the silver bullet that finally
ends the pandemic,

00:02:31.083 --> 00:02:32.551
and you just passed on it?

00:02:32.551 --> 00:02:34.721
"In my defense, I was
pretty high on bleach

00:02:34.721 --> 00:02:37.190
and hydroxychloroquine
during that meeting.

00:02:37.190 --> 00:02:38.891
And now experts are saying
we might be

00:02:38.891 --> 00:02:40.360
facing vaccine shortages.

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:42.461
I mean, I knew Trump was
a [bleep] businessman,

00:02:42.461 --> 00:02:44.464
but I didn't think
he was this bad.

00:02:44.464 --> 00:02:46.098
I'm starting to think
if you gave him a time machine,

00:02:46.098 --> 00:02:48.100
he'd go back to the year 2000
and buy stock

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:50.370
in apples and Enron.

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:52.371
I mean, what did you spend
that money on instead?

00:02:52.371 --> 00:02:54.373
The wall? Space Force?

00:02:54.373 --> 00:02:56.509
Discount hair dye
for Rudy Giuliani?

00:02:56.509 --> 00:02:59.145
"You can also use it to tar
your driveway. Win-win."

00:02:59.145 --> 00:03:01.447
Trump championed the vaccine
as the one thing he was doing

00:03:01.447 --> 00:03:04.250
to combat the virus,
and even that he [bleep] up.

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:07.086
It's like if The Flash showed up
to the Justice League

00:03:07.086 --> 00:03:08.654
with a pulled hamstring.
"You can't run?

00:03:08.654 --> 00:03:10.689
That's like your whole thing!"

00:03:10.689 --> 00:03:12.324
"Maybe I can help
with the plans?

00:03:12.324 --> 00:03:14.727
I have good ideas too, Batman!"

00:03:14.727 --> 00:03:16.896
And yet, during a White House
event yesterday,

00:03:16.896 --> 00:03:19.532
Trump still went out of his way
to pat himself on the back

00:03:19.532 --> 00:03:21.601
for the development
of the vaccine.

00:03:21.601 --> 00:03:25.571
-We're here to discuss a
monumental national achievement.

00:03:25.571 --> 00:03:29.275
From the instant the coronavirus
invaded our shores,

00:03:29.275 --> 00:03:32.178
we raced into action
to develop a safe

00:03:32.178 --> 00:03:35.147
and effective vaccine
at breakneck speed.

00:03:35.147 --> 00:03:37.716
It would normally take
five years, six years,

00:03:37.716 --> 00:03:39.452
seven years, or even more.

00:03:39.452 --> 00:03:42.521
Before Operation Warp Speed,
the typical time frame

00:03:42.521 --> 00:03:47.927
for development and approval,
as you know, could be infinity.

00:03:47.927 --> 00:03:51.531
-Yes, the old medical cliche --
could be infinity.

00:03:51.531 --> 00:03:53.766
I'll never forget when the
doctor told my grandpa

00:03:53.766 --> 00:03:57.003
he had between six months
and infinity to live.

00:03:57.003 --> 00:03:59.038
I also like when he says,
"as you know."

00:03:59.038 --> 00:04:01.840
Like we're all just going to nod
our heads and agree with him.

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:03.476
He'd be the [bleep] Jedi.

00:04:03.476 --> 00:04:06.278
"These aren't the droids you're
looking for, as you know."

00:04:06.278 --> 00:04:08.881
"Um, yeah, no, yeah,
they're right there.

00:04:08.881 --> 00:04:10.483
Step out of the land speeder,
sir."

00:04:10.483 --> 00:04:13.720
"Thanks for the help, droids.
Be-be-boo-boop to you!"

00:04:13.720 --> 00:04:15.988
[ Laughter ]

00:04:15.988 --> 00:04:18.524
He thinks he can just skate
past saying something insane

00:04:18.524 --> 00:04:19.959
and we'll all go for it.

00:04:19.959 --> 00:04:22.761
It's like if you asked your wife
about her day and she said,

00:04:22.761 --> 00:04:24.797
"Oh, paid some bills,
made a smoothie,

00:04:24.797 --> 00:04:27.567
the pool boy was here for a few
hours, went to the store,"

00:04:27.567 --> 00:04:30.469
and you said, "Wait.
We don't have a pool."

00:04:30.469 --> 00:04:32.672
But the best part came
in the middle of that event

00:04:32.672 --> 00:04:35.140
when the twin failures
of his presidency --

00:04:35.140 --> 00:04:37.075
his disastrous handling
of the pandemic

00:04:37.075 --> 00:04:39.678
and his historic loss
to Joe Biden collided at once.

00:04:39.678 --> 00:04:42.581
Because right in the middle
of his dumb, self-promoting,

00:04:42.581 --> 00:04:44.316
campaign-style vaccine event,

00:04:44.316 --> 00:04:47.019
the Supreme Court rejected
a desperate last-ditch effort

00:04:47.019 --> 00:04:49.822
by Republicans to stop
Pennsylvania from certifying

00:04:49.822 --> 00:04:51.557
its electoral votes
for Joe Biden.

00:04:51.557 --> 00:04:53.493
And Fox News,
of all the networks,

00:04:53.493 --> 00:04:55.428
had to break in during
live coverage

00:04:55.428 --> 00:04:59.364
of the Trump vaccine event
to report the devastating news.

00:04:59.364 --> 00:05:01.700
-I want to kick things off --
as I mentioned,

00:05:01.700 --> 00:05:03.369
there's a reason we asked you,

00:05:03.369 --> 00:05:05.838
in addition to
your general expertise

00:05:05.838 --> 00:05:07.673
and leadership, but it was
that the CDC --

00:05:07.673 --> 00:05:09.841
-Alright, we're momentarily
interrupting this to pass along

00:05:09.841 --> 00:05:12.445
some news that will be
distressing for the President.

00:05:12.445 --> 00:05:16.115
The U.S. Supreme Court has just
rejected a Republican challenge

00:05:16.115 --> 00:05:18.384
to Joe Biden's election win
in Pennsylvania.

00:05:18.384 --> 00:05:21.620
The Supreme Court has taken
a look at the request

00:05:21.620 --> 00:05:24.390
on the part of Republicans
to challenge that,

00:05:24.390 --> 00:05:26.825
to re-examine that.

00:05:26.825 --> 00:05:28.894
It has rejected that.

00:05:28.894 --> 00:05:30.630
The win stands.

00:05:30.630 --> 00:05:33.131
Joe Biden now clearly
the President-elect

00:05:33.131 --> 00:05:34.533
of the United States.

00:05:34.533 --> 00:05:36.269
Now back to the summit.

00:05:36.269 --> 00:05:38.003
-I mean, it's amazing.
I'm surprised Trump

00:05:38.003 --> 00:05:40.305
didn't look like post-failure
Wile E. Coyote

00:05:40.305 --> 00:05:42.307
when they cut back to him.

00:05:42.307 --> 00:05:44.743
His favorite network interrupted
what was supposed to be

00:05:44.743 --> 00:05:46.411
a celebration of his
greatest accomplishment

00:05:46.411 --> 00:05:48.514
to report the news that
the court that was supposed

00:05:48.514 --> 00:05:50.149
to help him steal the election,
which includes

00:05:50.149 --> 00:05:54.019
three of his own appointees,
had rejected his bid to overturn

00:05:54.019 --> 00:05:55.788
the results of an election
he lost.

00:05:55.788 --> 00:05:57.490
I'm not sure there's
a single moment

00:05:57.490 --> 00:05:59.258
that captures this farce
any better.

00:05:59.258 --> 00:06:01.093
It's like if halfway through
"Sesame Street,"

00:06:01.093 --> 00:06:03.128
Big Bird interrupted a song
about the alphabet,

00:06:03.128 --> 00:06:05.097
looked straight into
the camera and said,

00:06:05.097 --> 00:06:07.165
"Breaking news, kid,
no one likes you,

00:06:07.165 --> 00:06:09.135
and you're never going to learn
how to spell."

00:06:09.135 --> 00:06:10.803
Trump put three judges
on the Court,

00:06:10.803 --> 00:06:12.437
and he was very explicit
about the fact

00:06:12.437 --> 00:06:14.974
that he wanted them to jump in
and steal the election for him,

00:06:14.974 --> 00:06:17.309
Bush v. Gore style,
and he still lost.

00:06:17.309 --> 00:06:20.412
When those three saw the actual
court filing, it was probably

00:06:20.412 --> 00:06:23.149
like meeting someone you matched
with on Tinder in person.

00:06:23.149 --> 00:06:27.286
"So that picture you posted,
that was before the explosion?"

00:06:27.286 --> 00:06:28.754
The right-wing judges
on the Supreme Court

00:06:28.754 --> 00:06:30.055
are Trump superfans.

00:06:30.055 --> 00:06:31.390
They're desperate to side
with him.

00:06:31.390 --> 00:06:32.959
If he could have given
them a case

00:06:32.959 --> 00:06:34.660
with even a little meat on it,
they were ready to

00:06:34.660 --> 00:06:36.829
Hamburger Helper it
into a full meal,

00:06:36.829 --> 00:06:38.364
but there was nothing there.

00:06:38.364 --> 00:06:40.466
They had to admit it.
Although, I have to say,

00:06:40.466 --> 00:06:42.902
probably my favorite part
of this latest Trump

00:06:42.902 --> 00:06:46.138
legal face-plant is that
Texas Senator Ted Cruz

00:06:46.138 --> 00:06:49.341
offered very publicly
to present the oral arguments

00:06:49.341 --> 00:06:52.277
if the Court took the case,
in a sad attempt to curry favor

00:06:52.277 --> 00:06:53.679
with Trump and his voters.

00:06:53.679 --> 00:06:55.648
-Senator, let me applaud you,

00:06:55.648 --> 00:06:57.917
'cause you have offered
to step up.

00:06:57.917 --> 00:07:01.921
That to me is a slam dunk case
the Supreme Court should take.

00:07:01.921 --> 00:07:03.656
You're now willing
to argue that.

00:07:03.656 --> 00:07:06.659
-I believe the Supreme Court
should choose to take the case.

00:07:06.659 --> 00:07:08.627
I think they should hear
the appeal.

00:07:08.627 --> 00:07:12.832
And as you noted,
the legal team reached out

00:07:12.832 --> 00:07:16.268
and asked if I would be willing
to present the oral argument

00:07:16.268 --> 00:07:19.171
if the Court took the case,
and I told them I'd be happy to.

00:07:19.171 --> 00:07:21.640
-Now, I'm betting Ted Cruz
knew the Supreme Court

00:07:21.640 --> 00:07:23.943
wasn't going to take the case,
so he had nothing to lose

00:07:23.943 --> 00:07:26.144
by posturing and offering
to participate.

00:07:26.144 --> 00:07:28.381
Say what you will about
Ted Cruz, the man is crafty.

00:07:28.381 --> 00:07:31.383
As a rule, anytime you see
someone succeed

00:07:31.383 --> 00:07:34.319
despite reverse charisma,
they crafty.

00:07:34.319 --> 00:07:36.822
Although, it's a shame.
I would have loved to have seen

00:07:36.822 --> 00:07:38.824
knockoff General Zod in front
of the Supreme Court

00:07:38.824 --> 00:07:41.093
arguing that the election
results should be overturned

00:07:41.093 --> 00:07:43.529
in favor of a candidate
who attacked his wife

00:07:43.529 --> 00:07:45.864
and said his dad killed J.F.K.

00:07:45.864 --> 00:07:48.000
The only way it could have been
more pathetic is if Trump was

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:50.102
giving him a swirly
during the hearing.

00:07:50.102 --> 00:07:52.838
And then, of course, today after
the Supreme Court rejected

00:07:52.838 --> 00:07:54.873
this latest dumb lawsuit,
Trump tried to pretend

00:07:54.873 --> 00:07:57.243
he had nothing to do with it,
and that actually

00:07:57.243 --> 00:08:00.379
a new lawsuit filed by
the Texas attorney general

00:08:00.379 --> 00:08:02.948
was the real lawsuit
that would finally have

00:08:02.948 --> 00:08:04.717
all the proof
he's been promising

00:08:04.717 --> 00:08:06.219
of massive voter fraud.

00:08:06.219 --> 00:08:08.153
-This morning
the President tweeted,

00:08:08.153 --> 00:08:10.021
"Well, this was not my case."

00:08:10.021 --> 00:08:12.157
-He says the case that
everyone has been waiting for

00:08:12.157 --> 00:08:14.359
is the state's case with Texas.

00:08:14.359 --> 00:08:16.829
That's because Texas is now
suing other battlegrounds

00:08:16.829 --> 00:08:18.664
over their results.
-He wrote, quote,

00:08:18.664 --> 00:08:22.100
"We will be intervening
in the Texas case.

00:08:22.100 --> 00:08:24.169
This is the big one."

00:08:24.169 --> 00:08:27.473
-Oh, so this is the big one?
Not the 50 before it?

00:08:27.473 --> 00:08:29.909
This is like when in high school
when I tried to impress a date

00:08:29.909 --> 00:08:32.144
by winning her a stuffed animal
at the carnival, and it took me

00:08:32.144 --> 00:08:35.447
a bunch of tries, because
those things are rigged.

00:08:35.447 --> 00:08:37.416
And then when I asked the guy
running it if I could just

00:08:37.416 --> 00:08:39.518
buy the bear, he said,
"Those ain't the rules."

00:08:39.518 --> 00:08:41.587
And then I turned around,
only to find that Kelsey

00:08:41.587 --> 00:08:43.922
had long bailed on me.
Yeah.

00:08:43.922 --> 00:08:45.457
She went and met up
with Tyler Fletcher,

00:08:45.457 --> 00:08:46.692
which was always her plan.

00:08:46.692 --> 00:08:49.027
Turns out she only agreed
to go with me

00:08:49.027 --> 00:08:51.096
because her dad said,
"If I ever see that Fletcher boy

00:08:51.096 --> 00:08:53.099
rolling up here
in his BMW again, young lady,

00:08:53.099 --> 00:08:55.067
you'll be grounded
until graduation."

00:08:55.067 --> 00:08:59.571
So now, I'm there,
standing with no money,

00:08:59.571 --> 00:09:02.007
no bear,

00:09:02.007 --> 00:09:04.009
no Kelsey!

00:09:04.009 --> 00:09:06.679
Point is, Biden won!

00:09:06.679 --> 00:09:08.548
Let it go, dude!

00:09:10.048 --> 00:09:14.086
Now I got makeup
all over my hands.

00:09:14.086 --> 00:09:16.055
I guess it's not a surprise
Trump thinks he can just

00:09:16.055 --> 00:09:17.723
keep filing as many
lawsuits as he wants,

00:09:17.723 --> 00:09:19.391
since that's what he's done
his whole life.

00:09:19.391 --> 00:09:21.527
I mean, even before he became
president, he was involved

00:09:21.527 --> 00:09:25.898
in 3,500 lawsuits, so 50 is just
a drop in the bucket for him.

00:09:25.898 --> 00:09:28.567
It's like asking Tommy Chong
to take one hit off a bong,

00:09:28.567 --> 00:09:30.669
and then asking him,
"Do you feel anything yet?"

00:09:30.669 --> 00:09:33.238
Incidentally, the lawsuit
Trump is mentioning was brought

00:09:33.238 --> 00:09:35.741
by Texas Attorney General
Ken Paxton,

00:09:35.741 --> 00:09:37.710
a guy who was already
under criminal indictment

00:09:37.710 --> 00:09:39.845
for securities fraud
when seven of his aides

00:09:39.845 --> 00:09:41.880
called on law enforcement
to investigate him

00:09:41.880 --> 00:09:45.718
for bribery and abuse
of office in October.

00:09:45.718 --> 00:09:48.454
I guess he's angling for one of
those pardons Trump's doling out

00:09:48.454 --> 00:09:51.289
to friends and accomplices
the way your boss hands out

00:09:51.289 --> 00:09:54.159
$5 Starbucks gift cards
at the office holiday party.

00:09:54.159 --> 00:09:56.028
"Merry Christmas, enjoy
half a frappuccino on me.

00:09:56.028 --> 00:09:58.430
Half frap!"
Paxton wants the legislatures

00:09:58.430 --> 00:10:00.499
of four states
that went for Biden

00:10:00.499 --> 00:10:03.736
to just override the will
of their own citizens

00:10:03.736 --> 00:10:06.271
and give their electoral votes
to Trump,

00:10:06.271 --> 00:10:08.907
as he explained on
"Fox and Friends" this morning.

00:10:08.907 --> 00:10:12.144
-Ken, why is Texas getting
involved in this?

00:10:12.144 --> 00:10:14.680
-Well, these elections
in other states

00:10:14.680 --> 00:10:16.982
where state law was
not followed as required

00:10:16.982 --> 00:10:19.318
by the Constitution
affects my voters.

00:10:19.318 --> 00:10:22.855
Our argument is that
because these states,

00:10:22.855 --> 00:10:25.791
like Pennsylvania and Wisconsin,
did not follow

00:10:25.791 --> 00:10:28.426
their own state law,
and that these orders

00:10:28.426 --> 00:10:31.330
were by other elected officials
to change the law

00:10:31.330 --> 00:10:35.401
or by other judges,
that is unconstitutional.

00:10:35.401 --> 00:10:37.336
Therefore, that election...
-Right.

00:10:37.336 --> 00:10:39.337
-...we can't go back and fix it,
but we can say,

00:10:39.337 --> 00:10:42.207
"Okay, let's transfer this
to the legislature,

00:10:42.207 --> 00:10:44.142
which used to do this
in other states,

00:10:44.142 --> 00:10:46.812
and let them decide the outcome
of the election."

00:10:46.812 --> 00:10:49.081
-First of all, I always
assumed the unspoken part

00:10:49.081 --> 00:10:51.750
of "Don't mess with Texas"
is that Texas would, in turn,

00:10:51.750 --> 00:10:53.185
not mess with the rest of us.

00:10:53.185 --> 00:10:54.686
Second, I'm not sure
we should take advice

00:10:54.686 --> 00:10:56.988
about what the law says
from a guy who's already

00:10:56.988 --> 00:10:59.191
under criminal indictment,
and whose own aides

00:10:59.191 --> 00:11:01.927
say he should be investigated
for abuse of office.

00:11:01.927 --> 00:11:03.929
And not just one or two aides,

00:11:03.929 --> 00:11:06.231
seven of his aides
came out publicly

00:11:06.231 --> 00:11:08.300
and said Paxton broke the law.

00:11:08.300 --> 00:11:09.768
It's like an episode
of "Law &amp; Order"

00:11:09.768 --> 00:11:11.904
where Lennie Briscoe
knocks on a suspect's door,

00:11:11.904 --> 00:11:14.172
and all the neighbors
pour into the hallway and yell,

00:11:14.172 --> 00:11:15.441
"Yeah, that guy did it!"

00:11:15.441 --> 00:11:17.042
Third, the most horrifying thing

00:11:17.042 --> 00:11:19.544
about this whole charade
is the idea

00:11:19.544 --> 00:11:23.049
that the GOP doesn't just
want to invalidate

00:11:23.049 --> 00:11:24.416
the votes of millions
of Americans,

00:11:24.416 --> 00:11:27.152
they want state legislatures
to override them.

00:11:27.152 --> 00:11:29.255
That's why Trump has been
cold-calling officials

00:11:29.255 --> 00:11:30.722 line:0%
in Georgia, Michigan,
and Pennsylvania.

00:11:30.722 --> 00:11:33.025 line:0%
He's been asking them to
overturn the results

00:11:33.025 --> 00:11:34.293 line:0%
in their states.

00:11:34.293 --> 00:11:35.794
There's nothing you can say
about this

00:11:35.794 --> 00:11:37.930
other than the fact that it's
authoritarian behavior.

00:11:37.930 --> 00:11:40.332
They're actively trying to light
our democracy on fire.

00:11:40.332 --> 00:11:41.967
We need to state that plainly.

00:11:41.967 --> 00:11:43.802
The Republican Party and the
modern conservative movement

00:11:43.802 --> 00:11:46.371
are opposed to democracy
and want to destroy it.

00:11:46.371 --> 00:11:48.773
Just because Trump is
scream-tweeting at late night

00:11:48.773 --> 00:11:50.909
reruns of Sean Hannity
instead of rolling down

00:11:50.909 --> 00:11:53.979
Pennsylvania Avenue on a tank
in a bunch of designer scarves

00:11:53.979 --> 00:11:56.348
doesn't mean this isn't a coup.

00:11:56.348 --> 00:11:58.684
It's just a bad one, because
the people attempting it

00:11:58.684 --> 00:12:01.286
are traffic court lawyers
hired off Craigslist

00:12:01.286 --> 00:12:03.121
who got their law degrees
from DeVry,

00:12:03.121 --> 00:12:05.458 line:0%
or as we here
at "Late Night" call them,

00:12:05.458 --> 00:12:06.992 line:0%
the Kooky Cuckoo Coup Crew.

00:12:06.992 --> 00:12:08.561 line:0%
Which, very exciting news,

00:12:08.561 --> 00:12:10.128 line:0%
is going to be a new show
on Peacock starring

00:12:10.128 --> 00:12:11.964 line:0%
Kaley Cuoco, Ice-T, and Coco.

00:12:14.433 --> 00:12:17.636
That's what we get paid
the big bucks for.

00:12:17.636 --> 00:12:20.472
The simple, horrifying fact
is that it's now going to become

00:12:20.472 --> 00:12:22.808
canon in the right-wing
cinematic universe

00:12:22.808 --> 00:12:24.342
that Trump actually won
this election,

00:12:24.342 --> 00:12:26.779
and Biden is an
illegitimate president.

00:12:26.779 --> 00:12:29.815
That's why only 26 Congressional
Republicans are willing to say

00:12:29.815 --> 00:12:32.518
on the record that Biden is
the President-elect.

00:12:32.518 --> 00:12:35.387
It's why Republican leaders
shot down a simple resolution

00:12:35.387 --> 00:12:37.022
yesterday saying as much.

00:12:37.022 --> 00:12:39.491
It's why Republican wingnuts,
like Newt Gingrich,

00:12:39.491 --> 00:12:41.126
insist that any victory

00:12:41.126 --> 00:12:43.662
by their Democratic opponents
is illegitimate

00:12:43.662 --> 00:12:45.631
and must be the result of fraud.

00:12:45.631 --> 00:12:47.733
-The objective fact is,

00:12:47.733 --> 00:12:51.136
I believe Trump probably
did actually carry Georgia.

00:12:51.136 --> 00:12:54.306
I believe that the election
process is a mess.

00:12:54.306 --> 00:12:56.541
I really wish the governor
would call a special session

00:12:56.541 --> 00:12:58.243
to clean it up.

00:12:58.243 --> 00:13:00.246
And the Republicans simply
have to turn out

00:13:00.246 --> 00:13:03.982
more votes than
Stacey Abrams can steal.

00:13:03.982 --> 00:13:06.552
-Fox, I know you're scared
because you're losing viewers

00:13:06.552 --> 00:13:07.787
to Newsmax, but please,

00:13:07.787 --> 00:13:10.188
stop putting this racist
nut-sack on TV.

00:13:10.188 --> 00:13:12.458
In a medical textbooks,
Newt Gingrich Disease

00:13:12.458 --> 00:13:15.394
is what happens when you try
an epic skateboard trick

00:13:15.394 --> 00:13:17.930
and land nards-first
on the handrail.

00:13:17.930 --> 00:13:20.265
You think Stacey Abrams is
stealing votes?

00:13:20.265 --> 00:13:22.301
Trump's the one cold-calling
states trying to get them

00:13:22.301 --> 00:13:23.969
to overturn their results
like a telemarketer

00:13:23.969 --> 00:13:25.804
trying to get seniors
to fork over their

00:13:25.804 --> 00:13:28.007
Social Security numbers
for a free cruise.

00:13:28.007 --> 00:13:31.176
At this point, when Trump calls
a state lawmaker's iPhone,

00:13:31.176 --> 00:13:33.578
the number shows up
as "scam likely."

00:13:33.578 --> 00:13:35.580
Anyone who thinks this
will all just go away

00:13:35.580 --> 00:13:37.516
after Biden is sworn in
should think again.

00:13:37.516 --> 00:13:39.017
The modern Republican Party
is an unhinged

00:13:39.017 --> 00:13:41.654
authoritarian movement bent on
toppling our democracy

00:13:41.654 --> 00:13:43.388
in the service
of powerful interests

00:13:43.388 --> 00:13:44.590
and their wealthy patrons.

00:13:44.590 --> 00:13:46.825
Trump didn't create that,
he just revealed it

00:13:46.825 --> 00:13:49.294
and supercharged it, and
it will definitely outlast him,

00:13:49.294 --> 00:13:51.764
which is why we need serious,
far-reaching reforms

00:13:51.764 --> 00:13:53.432
to shore up
our institutions.

00:13:53.432 --> 00:13:56.034
Otherwise, this assault on
our democracy could go on

00:13:56.034 --> 00:13:59.371
for months or years or,
as experts say...

00:13:59.371 --> 00:14:00.605
-Could be infinity.

00:14:00.605 --> 00:14:02.441
-This has been "A Closer Look."

